      "id": "exact_after_apostrophe_normalization",
      "pins": "An apostrophe carries no word boundary, so `De'Andre` and `DeAndre` are one name and this is an EXACT match. Under the resolver's diagnostic normalization it is not - that spaces punctuation and leaves 'de andre' against 'deandre' - which is why linkage has its own key rather than borrowing that one.",
